  "duration": 48.118,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.321,
      "text": "The narwhal's famous unicorn horn is actually an erupted tooth.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "iNaturalist",
        "title": "Narwhal (Monodon monoceros)",
        "credit": "no rights reserved",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/178266310"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.333,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.321,
      "end": 10.416,
      "text": "When zoologists first inspected the Arctic whale, they found something baffling inside its mouth.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Narwalsch\u00e4del, Jagd- und Fischereimuseum in M\u00fcnchen.JPG",
        "credit": "High Contrast",
        "license": "CC BY 3.0 de",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Narwalsch%C3%A4del,_Jagd-_und_Fischereimuseum_in_M%C3%BCnchen.JPG"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.333,
          "end": 10.4,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "depth"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 10.416,
      "end": 15.611,
      "text": "Narwhals have no functional chewing teeth at all and swallow their deep-sea prey whole.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 10.4,
          "end": 15.6,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 15.611,
      "end": 21.981,
      "text": "Instead of eating with it, the male whale channels dental energy into a colossal upper left canine.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Narwhal.jpg",
        "credit": "AE Brehm",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Narwhal.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 15.6,
          "end": 21.967,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 21.981,
      "end": 28.151,
      "text": "This massive tusk can reach lengths of 1.5 to 3 meters in a counterclockwise spiral.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "The British miscellany, or, Coloured figures of new, rare, or little known animal subjects (Tab. 9) (6008286111).jpg",
        "credit": "Sowerby, James",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_British_miscellany,_or,_Coloured_figures_of_new,_rare,_or_little_known_animal_subjects_(Tab._9)_(6008286111).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 21.967,
          "end": 24.333,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 24.333,
          "end": 28.167,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "depth"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 28.151,
      "end": 36.026,
      "text": "Biologists discovered the giant external tooth is actually packed with millions of microscopic nerve endings.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 28.167,
          "end": 36.033,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 36.026,
      "end": 43.671,
      "text": "Because female narwhals usually lack tusks and still outlive males, the tusk is not needed for basic survival.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "The wild beasts of the world (Plate 36) (8116047765).jpg",
        "credit": "Finn, Frank",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_wild_beasts_of_the_world_(Plate_36)_(8116047765).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 36.033,
          "end": 43.667,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "depth"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
